  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "To complete the medium appropriate amounts of solutions B to G are added to the sterile solution A in the sequence as indicated."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Adjust pH of the medium to 6.5 - 7.0."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "Sparge solution A with 80% N2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture for 30 – 45 min to make it anoxic, distribute under same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "Solution B: Trace element solution SL-10"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "First dissolve FeCl2 in the HCl, then dilute in water, add and dissolve the other salts. Finally make up to 1000.0 ml."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": "Solutions B, D and G are autoclaved separately under 100% N2 gas."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 13,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": "Solution C: Seven vitamins solution"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 16,
      "comment": "Solutions C and F are prepared under 100% N2 gas and sterilized by filtration."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 17,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 18,
      "comment": "Solution D:  Selenite-tungstate solution"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 20,
      "comment": "Solutions B, D and G are autoclaved separately under 100% N2 gas."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 21,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 23,
      "comment": "Solution E is autoclaved under 80% N2 and 20% CO2 gas atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 24,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 25,
      "comment": "Solution F: Substrate solution (For DSM 15978)"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 27,
      "comment": "Use 2.00 g/l trimethylamine hydrochloride and 0.60 g/l methanol as substrates and adjust pH of the medium to 6.5 - 7.0."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 28,
      "comment": "After inoculation add 10.00 ml/l of a sterile anoxic stock solution of FeSO4 x 7 H2O (0.2% w/v)."
